<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://mr-bakhtawar.netlify.app/#website","url":"https://mr-bakhtawar.netlify.app/","name":"Mr. Bakhtawar Portfolio","description":"Official portfolio of Bakhtawar Khan (MBK), Founder of MBK Global, featuring digital projects, web development, AI, APIs and technical resources.","publisher":{"@id":"https://mr-bakhtawar.netlify.app/#person"},"inLanguage":"en"},{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://mr-bakhtawar.netlify.app/#person","name":"Bakhtawar Khan","alternateName":["Mr. Bakhtawar","Bakhtawar MBK","MBK Bakhtawar","Bakhtawar Khan","Bakhtawar Khan","MBK"],"url":"https://mr-bakhtawar.netlify.app/","image":"https://mr-bakhtawar.netlify.app/assets/images/gallery/muhammad-bakhtawar-khan-mbk-standing-professional-portrait.png","jobTitle":["Founder of MBK Global","Full-Stack Web Developer","Freelancer","Software Engineer","SEO Specialist"],"worksFor":{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https://mr-bakhtawar.netlify.app/#organization","name":"MBK Global","url":"https://mr-bakhtawar.netlify.app/"},"sameAs":["https://github.com/Muhammad-Bakhtawar-Khan","https://twitch.tv/mbk_bakhtawar"],"description":"Bakhtawar Khan, known online as Mr. Bakhtawar, Bakhtawar MBK and MBK Bakhtawar, is a Karachi-based full-stack web developer, freelancer, software engineer and SEO specialist. He is the founder of MBK Global and shares practical web projects and technology work."},{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https://mr-bakhtawar.netlify.app/#organization","name":"MBK Global","url":"https://mr-bakhtawar.netlify.app/","founder":{"@id":"https://mr-bakhtawar.netlify.app/#person"}},{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://mr-bakhtawar.netlify.app/faq.html#webpage","url":"https://mr-bakhtawar.netlify.app/faq.html","name":"FAQs | Bakhtawar Khan (MBK) Digital Services","description":"Answers about working with Bakhtawar Khan (MBK), project enquiries, web development, APIs, AI automation, SEO and the project delivery process.","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://mr-bakhtawar.netlify.app/#website"},"about":{"@id":"https://mr-bakhtawar.netlify.app/#person"},"inLanguage":"en"},{"@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://mr-bakhtawar.netlify.app/faq.html#faq","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What kind of projects can I discuss with you?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Website design and development, portfolio sites, landing pages, frontend improvements, API integrations, practical AI tools and workflow automation can be discussed based on project requirements. Explore selected projects ↗"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I request a quote?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Share your goals, the service you need, expected timeline and budget range through the project enquiry form. The more context you provide, the easier it is to understand scope and next steps. Open the enquiry form ↗"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How does the project process work?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"We begin with the goal and scope, agree on deliverables and timeline, then move through planning, design or implementation, review, agreed revisions and handover. View the project process ↗"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I see previous work or live demos?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Browse selected projects and case studies for available demos and context. Source code, live links and project details depend on what can be shared for each project. Browse case studies ↗"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do you work with clients remotely?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Remote collaboration can be discussed. Communication channels, milestones, working expectations and delivery dates should be agreed before work begins. Discuss collaboration ↗"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you help with SEO?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Technical SEO foundations such as page titles, metadata, canonical URLs, sitemap checks, internal links and indexing setup can be reviewed. Search rankings and indexing timelines cannot be guaranteed. Explore services ↗"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you build AI tools or connect APIs?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, share the workflow, systems or APIs involved, expected outcome and any data-security requirements. Feasibility depends on API access, usage limits and project scope. Explore technical resources ↗"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I contact you quickly?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Use the enquiry form to prepare a message with your details. WhatsApp opens with the message ready for review; you choose whether to send it. Contact Bakhtawar ↗"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Who is Bakhtawar Khan?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Bakhtawar Khan, also known as Bakhtawar Khan or MBK, is a digital professional and the founder of MBK Global. This portfolio documents his interests, projects and ongoing learning."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What does MBK stand for on this website?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"MBK is the short personal brand used by Bakhtawar Khan across this portfolio and related digital projects."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is MBK Global?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"MBK Global is the umbrella identity for digital projects, web experiences and technology experiments associated with Bakhtawar Khan. Project scope and availability can change as work develops."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where is Bakhtawar Khan based?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The portfolio identifies Bakhtawar Khan with Pakistan. For current availability and collaboration details, please use the contact page."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the purpose of this portfolio?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It brings together background information, selected projects, technical interests, resources and ways to contact Bakhtawar Khan."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How can I verify a project link?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Use the live project link listed on the portfolio and check the project’s own domain and content. If a link appears outdated, contact the portfolio owner."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does this portfolio guarantee search rankings?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. SEO work can improve technical accessibility and content clarity, but search engines decide indexing and rankings. No specific position or timeline is guaranteed."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you help improve an existing website?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Potentially. Share the website URL, goals, current problems and the changes you want. The recommended approach depends on the codebase and access available."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you create a personal portfolio website?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A portfolio can be scoped around biography, projects, skills, contact information, accessibility and SEO. Design and features should match the person’s real experience and goals."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you build a business website?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Business websites can include service pages, contact forms, location details, FAQs and relevant conversion paths. Requirements should be agreed before implementation."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you build an online store?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"An online store requires product data, checkout, payment-provider support, shipping rules, policies and security considerations. Feasibility depends on platform and scope."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can a website include appointment booking?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, if a suitable booking service or custom workflow is selected. Calendar rules, notifications, time zones and customer data handling should be defined first."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you add a training academy to a website?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"An academy may need course pages, enrolment, learner accounts, progress tracking and payments. The exact feature set should be planned around the learning model."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you integrate third-party APIs?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"API integration can connect a website to an external service when valid credentials, documentation, permissions and acceptable usage limits are available."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What information is needed for an API project?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Share the API documentation, desired user flow, authentication method, expected traffic, error cases and whether any sensitive data is involved. Never send passwords or secret keys in public messages."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you build an AI-powered feature?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"AI features can be explored when the task, input data, expected output, evaluation criteria and budget for API usage are clear."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you automate repetitive work?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Automation may connect forms, spreadsheets, notifications and business tools. First map the current steps, exceptions, permissions and what should happen when a step fails."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you build a WhatsApp bot?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A WhatsApp automation project depends on the chosen provider, approved APIs, messaging policies, user consent and the intended conversation flow."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is technical SEO?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Technical SEO focuses on making a site easier for search engines to crawl and understand, including indexability, canonical URLs, metadata, structured data, internal links and sitemaps."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do meta keywords improve Google rankings?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Google Search does not use the meta keywords tag for web ranking. Clear page content, titles, links and technical accessibility are more useful priorities."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How should page titles be written?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Use a unique, concise title that accurately describes the page and naturally includes the main topic or entity. Avoid repetitive keyword stuffing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What makes a good meta description?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A helpful description summarises the actual page in natural language and gives searchers a clear reason to visit. Search engines may choose a different snippet."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is a canonical URL?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A canonical URL signals the preferred version of similar or duplicate pages. It should point to the correct live URL and be consistent with internal links and sitemaps."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is an XML sitemap?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"An XML sitemap lists canonical URLs that a site owner wants search engines to discover. It does not guarantee indexing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What does robots.txt do?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The robots.txt file gives crawlers instructions about crawling paths. It is not a reliable way to keep private information out of search results."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How can I check whether a page is indexed?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Use Google Search Console URL Inspection for the exact live URL. A page being crawlable does not automatically mean it will be indexed."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why might Google show the wrong snippet?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Google may generate snippets from page text or choose a different title based on the query. Keep visible content, title tags and metadata accurate and consistent."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why might a page not appear for my full name?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Search visibility depends on competition, relevance, indexing, links and how clearly the site identifies the person. Ranking changes are not immediate or guaranteed."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Should every page link to every other page?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Link pages where the destination is genuinely useful. A clear navigation menu and contextual links are better than repeating the same links excessively."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How many FAQs should a website have?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Add questions that real visitors need answered. A large FAQ can help users when it stays accurate and organised, but volume alone does not improve rankings."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Should FAQ structured data be added?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Structured data must match visible page content and follow current search-engine policies. Valid markup does not guarantee a rich result."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is image SEO?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Image SEO includes descriptive filenames, useful alt text, appropriate formats, responsive sizing, compression and placing images near relevant content."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How should alt text be written?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Describe the meaningful information conveyed by the image in context. Avoid stuffing names and keywords or repeating nearby captions unnecessarily."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Should decorative images have alt text?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Purely decorative images should generally use an empty alt attribute so assistive technology can skip them."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can images help people find my profile?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Well-labelled, relevant images can improve accessibility and image discovery, but search visibility depends on many factors and cannot be promised."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is structured data?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Structured data is machine-readable markup that describes page entities or content. It must be accurate, visible where required and consistent with the page."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the difference between SEO and AEO?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"SEO helps content be discovered in search engines. AEO is a broad term for structuring useful answers clearly for answer-oriented search experiences; neither guarantees placement."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What does GEO mean in digital content?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"GEO is often used to describe making information clear and citable in generative search experiences. Strong factual content and clear entity information are sensible foundations, not a guarantee."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you help with website accessibility?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Accessibility improvements can include semantic headings, keyboard navigation, visible focus, sufficient contrast, meaningful labels and descriptive link text."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why is mobile responsiveness important?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Responsive layouts help content and controls work across different screen sizes and support a more usable experience on phones and tablets."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How can a website load faster?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Common improvements include compressing images, reducing unnecessary scripts, caching assets, limiting heavy third-party code and measuring real performance."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do you use a particular framework?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The portfolio demonstrates work across web technologies such as HTML, CSS, JavaScript and React. The best stack depends on project requirements and maintenance needs."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you work with existing HTML and CSS?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, improvements can be planned around existing code after reviewing its structure, dependencies, visual design and deployment process."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you help with React projects?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"React work can include components, page layouts, state handling, accessibility, performance and API integration, depending on the existing project."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you help debug a website?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Share a reproducible issue, browser or device details, relevant error messages and the expected behaviour. Remove secrets and personal data before sharing logs."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you review website security?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A scoped review may cover common web risks and safer implementation practices. A proper security assessment needs explicit authorisation and a clearly agreed scope."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is responsible reverse engineering?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Reverse engineering can be used to understand software behaviour where legally authorised. Work must respect applicable law, licences, privacy and system-owner permissions."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you test a website I do not own?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Only with explicit permission from the owner. Testing should stay within an agreed scope and must not disrupt services or access data without authorisation."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How should API keys be protected?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Keep secrets on the server or in a secure environment manager, rotate exposed keys, apply least-privilege permissions and never commit credentials to public repositories."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is HTTPS?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"HTTPS encrypts data exchanged between a browser and a website and helps verify the site’s server identity. It does not by itself make every site feature secure."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do you provide cloud or VPS setup?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Cloud and VPS tasks can be discussed around operating system, access controls, backups, updates, monitoring and budget. Exact requirements determine the approach."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the difference between VPS and shared hosting?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A VPS generally provides a more isolated virtual server environment, while shared hosting places multiple sites in a managed environment. The right choice depends on needs and administration skills."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you help with domain setup?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Domain configuration can involve DNS records, hosting targets, redirects and email records. Changes should be verified carefully to avoid interrupting existing services."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you deploy a website on Vercel?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Static and supported web applications can be deployed on Vercel when build settings, environment variables and project configuration are correct."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you help with GitHub?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"GitHub workflows may include repository organisation, commits, branches, pull requests, deployment connections and troubleshooting build failures."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What should a project brief include?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Include the problem, target audience, key pages, required features, examples, content availability, budget range, timeline and who will approve the work."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How are project timelines decided?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Timelines depend on complexity, content readiness, integrations, review cycles and third-party services. A realistic schedule should be agreed after scope is understood."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do you offer revisions?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Revision rounds and what counts as a revision should be agreed before work starts so expectations remain clear."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I request changes after launch?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Post-launch changes can be scoped separately. Keep a list of issues, priorities and desired outcomes to make follow-up work efficient."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Who provides website text and images?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Responsibilities for copy, brand assets, photography and licensing should be agreed at the start. Any supplied assets should be cleared for use."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you use my existing logo?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"An existing logo can usually be incorporated if you have the rights to use it and provide a suitable file format."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you help with branding?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Digital branding may include visual consistency, messaging, typography, colours and profile presentation, based on the existing identity and project goals."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you create social profile links?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A profile page can link to verified social accounts. Only accounts that belong to the person or brand should be represented as official."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where can I find Bakhtawar Khan online?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"You can visit the About.me profile at about.me/muhammadbakhtawar and the Linktree page at linktr.ee/bakhtawark085, alongside the verified profiles listed on this site."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the About.me profile for?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The About.me page provides another public profile destination for Bakhtawar Khan. Keep its biography and links consistent with the main portfolio."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the Linktree page for?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The Linktree page can collect selected profile and project links in one place. Check that each destination is current and correctly labelled."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is MBK TV?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"MBK TV is one of the digital projects associated with the MBK portfolio. Visit its live site for current features and availability."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is MBK Markets?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"MBK Markets is a project exploring a market-data interface. It should not be treated as financial advice or a promise of investment performance."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is MBK Downloader?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"MBK Downloader is listed among the portfolio’s web-tool projects. Use services lawfully and respect copyright, platform terms and privacy."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is Noor-e-Quran by MBK?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Noor-e-Quran is a faith-related digital project associated with the portfolio. Users should verify religious quotations and references against trusted sources."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is Text to Handwriting?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Text to Handwriting is a tool concept that presents typed text in a handwriting-like style. Output quality and available features depend on the current live version."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are all projects production-ready?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not necessarily. Some entries may be experiments or works in progress. Check each project’s live page for its current state and capabilities."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you collaborate with another developer?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Collaboration can be discussed when responsibilities, communication, ownership, review process and deadlines are clear."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you work with international clients?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Remote collaboration may be possible. Time zones, payment arrangements, scope, communication and legal requirements should be discussed before commitment."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What languages can project content use?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Language requirements should be specified early. Multilingual websites may need translated content, language navigation and appropriate page metadata."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you make a website bilingual?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A bilingual website can be planned with translated content, clear language switching and appropriate URL and metadata strategies for each language."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How should contact forms handle personal data?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Collect only necessary information, explain how it will be used, protect submissions and provide an appropriate privacy notice."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you add analytics?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Analytics can be considered when the measurement goals, privacy obligations and consent requirements are understood. Avoid collecting unnecessary personal information."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is a privacy policy?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A privacy policy explains what personal information is collected, why it is processed, how it is stored or shared and what choices people have."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you add a cookie banner?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A consent interface may be needed depending on the technologies used and applicable laws. It should reflect actual tracking behaviour rather than be purely decorative."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How should website testimonials be used?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Publish testimonials only with permission and ensure they reflect real feedback. Do not invent reviewers, identities, ratings or customer experiences."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I leave feedback on a project?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Feedback can be shared through the contact page. Please identify the relevant project and describe what worked well or what should improve."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What does human rights mean online?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Digital human rights include privacy, freedom of expression, access to information, non-discrimination and safety, subject to applicable law and the rights of others."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How can websites respect human rights?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Use privacy-conscious design, accessible content, clear policies, secure handling of data and respectful moderation. Avoid deceptive patterns and discriminatory treatment."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why is digital privacy important?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Personal information can reveal sensitive details. Collecting less data, limiting access and explaining data use help reduce unnecessary privacy risks."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is responsible AI use?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Responsible AI use involves checking outputs, protecting sensitive data, being transparent about limitations and considering bias, safety and human oversight."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How can a website be more inclusive?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Use accessible markup, readable language, keyboard support, sufficient contrast, responsive layouts and respectful content that does not exclude groups of users."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do you handle project confidentiality?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Discuss confidentiality needs before sharing sensitive information. Do not send passwords, private keys, identity documents or confidential customer data through public channels."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What happens if a third-party API changes?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"External APIs can change or become unavailable. Robust projects should handle errors, document dependencies and plan for maintenance when necessary."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do you test a website before launch?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Testing can include mobile and desktop layouts, links, forms, keyboard use, accessibility basics, performance, metadata, redirects and key user journeys."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What should be checked after a site launches?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Verify the live domain, HTTPS, redirects, page rendering, analytics if used, sitemap, robots rules, forms and Search Console status."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you guarantee a website will never go down?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Hosting providers, networks, code and third-party services can fail. Monitoring, backups and recovery planning can reduce risk but not eliminate it."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How often should website content be updated?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Update content when facts, services, project links or policies change. Accuracy and usefulness matter more than publishing on an arbitrary schedule."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I report a broken link?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Send the page URL, the broken destination and what you expected to find through the contact page."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How can I contact Bakhtawar Khan?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Use the contact page or project enquiry form. Include a short description, relevant links and the best way to respond."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What should I include in a first message?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Explain who you are, what you want to achieve, the current situation, important constraints and any deadline. Avoid sending credentials or sensitive personal data."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I know if a project is a good fit?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A good fit has a clearly described problem, realistic scope, available inputs, agreed responsibilities and a shared understanding of budget and timing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do you promise a specific result?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No result should be promised before requirements and constraints are understood. Search rankings, traffic, conversion rates and third-party uptime are outside any single developer’s full control."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How can I keep learning web development?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Build small projects, read official documentation, test your assumptions, review errors and improve one part of a project at a time."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How can I contribute to an open-source project?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Read the project’s licence and contribution guide, reproduce an issue, make a focused change and explain what you tested."}}]}]}</script>
<meta content="Bakhtawar Khan, Bakhtawar Khan, MBK, MBK Global, Bakhtawar developer, MBK developer, personal portfolio Karachi Pakistan, web development portfolio, AI and API integration, technical SEO, answer engine optimization (AEO), generative engine optimization (GEO), website security, digital branding, automation workflows, web performance optimization, structured data SEO, personal brand SEO" name="keywords"><meta content="Mr. Bakhtawar (Bakhtawar Khan)" name="author">

<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com"><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin=""><link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&amp;family=Manrope:wght@400;500;600;700;800&amp;display=swap" rel="stylesheet"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/academy.css"><script defer src="/assets/js/academy.js"></script><script>(function(){try{var t=localStorage.getItem('portfolio-theme');document.documentElement.dataset.theme=t||(matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches?'dark':'light')}catch(e){}})()</script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/portfolio.css"><meta property="og:site_name" content="Mr. Bakhtawar Portfolio"><meta property="og:image" content="https://mr-bakhtawar.netlify.app/assets/images/bakhtawar-portfolio-social-v1.png"><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://mr-bakhtawar.netlify.app/assets/images/bakhtawar-portfolio-social-v1.png"><meta property="og:image:alt" content="Mr. Bakhtawar Portfolio — Bakhtawar Khan. Personal Digital Portfolio · MBK Global."><meta name="twitter:image:alt" content="Mr. Bakhtawar Portfolio — Bakhtawar Khan. Personal Digital Portfolio · MBK Global."><meta property="og:image:width" content="1200"><meta property="og:image:height" content="630"><meta property="og:image:type" content="image/png"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta property="og:title" content="Frequently Asked Questions | Mr. Bakhtawar"><meta name="twitter:title" content="Frequently Asked Questions | Mr. Bakhtawar"><meta property="og:description" content="FAQs: A practical guide to projects, services, timelines and working together. Find what you need, then let's make your next idea happen. By Mr. Bakhtawar."><meta name="twitter:description" content="FAQs: A practical guide to projects, services, timelines and working together. Find what you need, then let's make your next idea happen. By Mr. Bakhtawar."><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/identity.css"><link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/assets/images/portfolio-icon-180.png"><link rel="manifest" href="/site.webmanifest"></head><body data-page="faq.html" class="academy page-faq"><header class="academy-header" id="top"><a class="academy-brand personal-brand" href="/"><span>Bakhtawar Khan<small>Personal Digital Portfolio · MBK Global</small></span></a><button class="academy-menu" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="academy-nav">Menu <span>+</span></button><nav id="academy-nav" aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="/">Home</a><a href='/about'>About</a><a href='/projects'>Projects</a><a href='/services'>Services</a><a class='header-cta' href='/hire-me'>Let’s talk <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><details class="portfolio-more"><summary>More</summary><div class="portfolio-panel"><section><h2>Professional work</h2><a href='/case-studies'>Case Studies</a><a href='/changelog'>Projects Changelog</a><a href='/delivered-project'>Process</a><a href='/resources'>Resources</a><a href='/news'>Notes</a></section><section><h2>Contact &amp; career</h2><a href='/book-a-call'>Book a Call</a><a href='/resume'>Resume / CV</a><a href='/hire-me'>Hire Me</a></section><section><h2>Content &amp; media</h2><a href='/gallery'>Gallery</a><a href='/blog'>Blog &amp; Articles</a><a href='/faq'>FAQs</a></section><section><h2>Personal brand</h2><a href='/about-muhammad-bakhtawar-khan'>Founder Profile</a><a href='/social'>Social Profiles</a><a href='/official-links'>Official Links</a></section></div></details><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" aria-label="Switch color theme">◐</button></nav></header>
<a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a><main class="wrap inner-page faq-page academy-main" id="main-content"><section class="academy-page-hero"><div class="academy-breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href='/resources'>Explore MBK</a></div><div class="academy-kicker">faq <span> / MBK GLOBAL</span></div><h1 class="page-title" id="faq-title">Good questions.<br><em>Clear answers.</em></h1><p class="intro">A practical guide to projects, services, timelines and working together. Find what you need, then let's make your next idea happen.</p></section>
<section aria-labelledby="faq-title" class="faq-hero">
<div class="faq-hero-copy">
<p class="eyebrow"><span class="faq-status-dot"></span> MBK HELP CENTRE / FAQ</p>


<div class="faq-hero-actions"><a class='button button-primary' href='/contact#project-enquiry'>Start a project <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class='text-link' href='/services'>Explore services <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
<div class="faq-proof-row"><div><strong>01</strong><span>Clear scope</span></div><div><strong>02</strong><span>Open communication</span></div><div><strong>03</strong><span>Practical delivery</span></div></div>
</div>
<aside aria-label="Quick help" class="faq-hero-card">
<div class="faq-card-mark">?</div><p class="eyebrow">NEED A QUICK ANSWER?</p><h2 id="section-1">Start with the essentials.</h2><p>Search the questions or choose a topic. If your situation is unique, send a project enquiry and include a few details.</p><a class='faq-card-link' href='/contact#project-enquiry'>Talk about your project <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
<div class="faq-card-foot"><span class="faq-status-dot"></span> Remote enquiries welcome</div>
</aside>
</section>
<section aria-label="Frequently asked questions" class="faq-workspace">
<div class="faq-workspace-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE KNOW-HOW</p><h2 id="section-2">Find your <em>answer.</em></h2></div><p>Choose a topic or search by keyword.</p></div>
<div class="faq-controls"><label class="faq-search"><span aria-hidden="true">⌕</span><input aria-label="Search frequently asked questions" id="faqSearch" placeholder="Search questions…" type="search"><kbd>⌕</kbd></label><div aria-label="Filter questions by topic" class="faq-filters" role="group"><button aria-pressed="true" class="faq-filter is-active" data-filter="all" type="button">All topics <span>108</span></button><button aria-pressed="false" class="faq-filter" data-filter="projects" type="button">Projects</button><button aria-pressed="false" class="faq-filter" data-filter="services" type="button">Services</button><button aria-pressed="false" class="faq-filter" data-filter="process" type="button">Process</button></div></div>
<div aria-live="polite" class="faq-results-note" id="faqResults">Showing all 108 answers</div>
<div class="faq-list faq-list-premium" id="faqList">
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">01 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>What kind of projects can I discuss with you?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Website design and development, portfolio sites, landing pages, frontend improvements, API integrations, practical AI tools and workflow automation can be discussed based on project requirements.</p><a href='/projects'>Explore selected projects ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">02 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>How do I request a quote?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Share your goals, the service you need, expected timeline and budget range through the project enquiry form. The more context you provide, the easier it is to understand scope and next steps.</p><a href='/contact#project-enquiry'>Open the enquiry form ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="process"><div class="faq-item-index">03 <span>PROCESS</span></div><details><summary>How does the project process work?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>We begin with the goal and scope, agree on deliverables and timeline, then move through planning, design or implementation, review, agreed revisions and handover.</p><a href='/delivered-project'>View the project process ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">04 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>Can I see previous work or live demos?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. Browse selected projects and case studies for available demos and context. Source code, live links and project details depend on what can be shared for each project.</p><a href='/case-studies'>Browse case studies ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="process"><div class="faq-item-index">05 <span>PROCESS</span></div><details><summary>Do you work with clients remotely?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Remote collaboration can be discussed. Communication channels, milestones, working expectations and delivery dates should be agreed before work begins.</p><a href='/contact'>Discuss collaboration ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="services"><div class="faq-item-index">06 <span>SERVICES</span></div><details><summary>Can you help with SEO?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Technical SEO foundations such as page titles, metadata, canonical URLs, sitemap checks, internal links and indexing setup can be reviewed. Search rankings and indexing timelines cannot be guaranteed.</p><a href='/services'>Explore services ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="services"><div class="faq-item-index">07 <span>SERVICES</span></div><details><summary>Can you build AI tools or connect APIs?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes, share the workflow, systems or APIs involved, expected outcome and any data-security requirements. Feasibility depends on API access, usage limits and project scope.</p><a href='/resources'>Explore technical resources ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="process"><div class="faq-item-index">08 <span>PROCESS</span></div><details><summary>How do I contact you quickly?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Use the enquiry form to prepare a message with your details. WhatsApp opens with the message ready for review; you choose whether to send it.</p><a href='/contact#project-enquiry'>Contact Bakhtawar ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">008 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>Who is Bakhtawar Khan?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Bakhtawar Khan, also known as Bakhtawar Khan or MBK, is a digital professional and the founder of MBK Global. This portfolio documents his interests, projects and ongoing learning.</p><a href='/about'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">009 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>What does MBK stand for on this website?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>MBK is the short personal brand used by Bakhtawar Khan across this portfolio and related digital projects.</p><a href='/about'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">010 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>What is MBK Global?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>MBK Global is the umbrella identity for digital projects, web experiences and technology experiments associated with Bakhtawar Khan. Project scope and availability can change as work develops.</p><a href='/about'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">011 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>Where is Bakhtawar Khan based?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>The portfolio identifies Bakhtawar Khan with Pakistan. For current availability and collaboration details, please use the contact page.</p><a href='/about'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">012 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>What is the purpose of this portfolio?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>It brings together background information, selected projects, technical interests, resources and ways to contact Bakhtawar Khan.</p><a href='/about'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">013 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>How can I verify a project link?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Use the live project link listed on the portfolio and check the project’s own domain and content. If a link appears outdated, contact the portfolio owner.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">014 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>Does this portfolio guarantee search rankings?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>No. SEO work can improve technical accessibility and content clarity, but search engines decide indexing and rankings. No specific position or timeline is guaranteed.</p><a href='/about'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">015 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>Can you help improve an existing website?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Potentially. Share the website URL, goals, current problems and the changes you want. The recommended approach depends on the codebase and access available.</p><a href='/services'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">016 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>Can you create a personal portfolio website?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>A portfolio can be scoped around biography, projects, skills, contact information, accessibility and SEO. Design and features should match the person’s real experience and goals.</p><a href='/about'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">017 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>Can you build a business website?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Business websites can include service pages, contact forms, location details, FAQs and relevant conversion paths. Requirements should be agreed before implementation.</p><a href='/services'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">018 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>Can you build an online store?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>An online store requires product data, checkout, payment-provider support, shipping rules, policies and security considerations. Feasibility depends on platform and scope.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">019 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>Can a website include appointment booking?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes, if a suitable booking service or custom workflow is selected. Calendar rules, notifications, time zones and customer data handling should be defined first.</p><a href='/services'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">020 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>Can you add a training academy to a website?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>An academy may need course pages, enrolment, learner accounts, progress tracking and payments. The exact feature set should be planned around the learning model.</p><a href='/services'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">021 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>Can you integrate third-party APIs?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>API integration can connect a website to an external service when valid credentials, documentation, permissions and acceptable usage limits are available.</p><a href='/services'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">022 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>What information is needed for an API project?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Share the API documentation, desired user flow, authentication method, expected traffic, error cases and whether any sensitive data is involved. Never send passwords or secret keys in public messages.</p><a href='/services'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">023 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>Can you build an AI-powered feature?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>AI features can be explored when the task, input data, expected output, evaluation criteria and budget for API usage are clear.</p><a href='/services'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">024 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>Can you automate repetitive work?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Automation may connect forms, spreadsheets, notifications and business tools. First map the current steps, exceptions, permissions and what should happen when a step fails.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">025 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>Can you build a WhatsApp bot?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>A WhatsApp automation project depends on the chosen provider, approved APIs, messaging policies, user consent and the intended conversation flow.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">026 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>What is technical SEO?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Technical SEO focuses on making a site easier for search engines to crawl and understand, including indexability, canonical URLs, metadata, structured data, internal links and sitemaps.</p><a href='/services'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">027 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>Do meta keywords improve Google rankings?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Google Search does not use the meta keywords tag for web ranking. Clear page content, titles, links and technical accessibility are more useful priorities.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="services"><div class="faq-item-index">028 <span>SERVICES</span></div><details><summary>How should page titles be written?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Use a unique, concise title that accurately describes the page and naturally includes the main topic or entity. Avoid repetitive keyword stuffing.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="services"><div class="faq-item-index">029 <span>SERVICES</span></div><details><summary>What makes a good meta description?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>A helpful description summarises the actual page in natural language and gives searchers a clear reason to visit. Search engines may choose a different snippet.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="services"><div class="faq-item-index">030 <span>SERVICES</span></div><details><summary>What is a canonical URL?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>A canonical URL signals the preferred version of similar or duplicate pages. It should point to the correct live URL and be consistent with internal links and sitemaps.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="services"><div class="faq-item-index">031 <span>SERVICES</span></div><details><summary>What is an XML sitemap?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>An XML sitemap lists canonical URLs that a site owner wants search engines to discover. It does not guarantee indexing.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="services"><div class="faq-item-index">032 <span>SERVICES</span></div><details><summary>What does robots.txt do?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>The robots.txt file gives crawlers instructions about crawling paths. It is not a reliable way to keep private information out of search results.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="services"><div class="faq-item-index">033 <span>SERVICES</span></div><details><summary>How can I check whether a page is indexed?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Use Google Search Console URL Inspection for the exact live URL. A page being crawlable does not automatically mean it will be indexed.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="services"><div class="faq-item-index">034 <span>SERVICES</span></div><details><summary>Why might Google show the wrong snippet?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Google may generate snippets from page text or choose a different title based on the query. Keep visible content, title tags and metadata accurate and consistent.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="services"><div class="faq-item-index">035 <span>SERVICES</span></div><details><summary>Why might a page not appear for my full name?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Search visibility depends on competition, relevance, indexing, links and how clearly the site identifies the person. Ranking changes are not immediate or guaranteed.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="services"><div class="faq-item-index">036 <span>SERVICES</span></div><details><summary>Should every page link to every other page?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>No. Link pages where the destination is genuinely useful. A clear navigation menu and contextual links are better than repeating the same links excessively.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="services"><div class="faq-item-index">037 <span>SERVICES</span></div><details><summary>How many FAQs should a website have?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Add questions that real visitors need answered. A large FAQ can help users when it stays accurate and organised, but volume alone does not improve rankings.</p><a href='/services'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="services"><div class="faq-item-index">038 <span>SERVICES</span></div><details><summary>Should FAQ structured data be added?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Structured data must match visible page content and follow current search-engine policies. Valid markup does not guarantee a rich result.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="services"><div class="faq-item-index">039 <span>SERVICES</span></div><details><summary>What is image SEO?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Image SEO includes descriptive filenames, useful alt text, appropriate formats, responsive sizing, compression and placing images near relevant content.</p><a href='/services'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="services"><div class="faq-item-index">040 <span>SERVICES</span></div><details><summary>How should alt text be written?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Describe the meaningful information conveyed by the image in context. Avoid stuffing names and keywords or repeating nearby captions unnecessarily.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="services"><div class="faq-item-index">041 <span>SERVICES</span></div><details><summary>Should decorative images have alt text?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Purely decorative images should generally use an empty alt attribute so assistive technology can skip them.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="services"><div class="faq-item-index">042 <span>SERVICES</span></div><details><summary>Can images help people find my profile?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Well-labelled, relevant images can improve accessibility and image discovery, but search visibility depends on many factors and cannot be promised.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="services"><div class="faq-item-index">043 <span>SERVICES</span></div><details><summary>What is structured data?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Structured data is machine-readable markup that describes page entities or content. It must be accurate, visible where required and consistent with the page.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="services"><div class="faq-item-index">044 <span>SERVICES</span></div><details><summary>What is the difference between SEO and AEO?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>SEO helps content be discovered in search engines. AEO is a broad term for structuring useful answers clearly for answer-oriented search experiences; neither guarantees placement.</p><a href='/services'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="services"><div class="faq-item-index">045 <span>SERVICES</span></div><details><summary>What does GEO mean in digital content?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>GEO is often used to describe making information clear and citable in generative search experiences. Strong factual content and clear entity information are sensible foundations, not a guarantee.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="services"><div class="faq-item-index">046 <span>SERVICES</span></div><details><summary>Can you help with website accessibility?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Accessibility improvements can include semantic headings, keyboard navigation, visible focus, sufficient contrast, meaningful labels and descriptive link text.</p><a href='/services'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="services"><div class="faq-item-index">047 <span>SERVICES</span></div><details><summary>Why is mobile responsiveness important?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Responsive layouts help content and controls work across different screen sizes and support a more usable experience on phones and tablets.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="services"><div class="faq-item-index">048 <span>SERVICES</span></div><details><summary>How can a website load faster?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Common improvements include compressing images, reducing unnecessary scripts, caching assets, limiting heavy third-party code and measuring real performance.</p><a href='/services'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="services"><div class="faq-item-index">049 <span>SERVICES</span></div><details><summary>Do you use a particular framework?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>The portfolio demonstrates work across web technologies such as HTML, CSS, JavaScript and React. The best stack depends on project requirements and maintenance needs.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="services"><div class="faq-item-index">050 <span>SERVICES</span></div><details><summary>Can you work with existing HTML and CSS?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes, improvements can be planned around existing code after reviewing its structure, dependencies, visual design and deployment process.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="services"><div class="faq-item-index">051 <span>SERVICES</span></div><details><summary>Can you help with React projects?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>React work can include components, page layouts, state handling, accessibility, performance and API integration, depending on the existing project.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="services"><div class="faq-item-index">052 <span>SERVICES</span></div><details><summary>Can you help debug a website?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Share a reproducible issue, browser or device details, relevant error messages and the expected behaviour. Remove secrets and personal data before sharing logs.</p><a href='/services'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="services"><div class="faq-item-index">053 <span>SERVICES</span></div><details><summary>Can you review website security?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>A scoped review may cover common web risks and safer implementation practices. A proper security assessment needs explicit authorisation and a clearly agreed scope.</p><a href='/services'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="services"><div class="faq-item-index">054 <span>SERVICES</span></div><details><summary>What is responsible reverse engineering?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Reverse engineering can be used to understand software behaviour where legally authorised. Work must respect applicable law, licences, privacy and system-owner permissions.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="services"><div class="faq-item-index">055 <span>SERVICES</span></div><details><summary>Can you test a website I do not own?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Only with explicit permission from the owner. Testing should stay within an agreed scope and must not disrupt services or access data without authorisation.</p><a href='/services'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="services"><div class="faq-item-index">056 <span>SERVICES</span></div><details><summary>How should API keys be protected?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Keep secrets on the server or in a secure environment manager, rotate exposed keys, apply least-privilege permissions and never commit credentials to public repositories.</p><a href='/services'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="services"><div class="faq-item-index">057 <span>SERVICES</span></div><details><summary>What is HTTPS?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>HTTPS encrypts data exchanged between a browser and a website and helps verify the site’s server identity. It does not by itself make every site feature secure.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="process"><div class="faq-item-index">058 <span>PROCESS</span></div><details><summary>Do you provide cloud or VPS setup?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Cloud and VPS tasks can be discussed around operating system, access controls, backups, updates, monitoring and budget. Exact requirements determine the approach.</p><a href='/services'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="process"><div class="faq-item-index">059 <span>PROCESS</span></div><details><summary>What is the difference between VPS and shared hosting?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>A VPS generally provides a more isolated virtual server environment, while shared hosting places multiple sites in a managed environment. The right choice depends on needs and administration skills.</p><a href='/services'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="process"><div class="faq-item-index">060 <span>PROCESS</span></div><details><summary>Can you help with domain setup?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Domain configuration can involve DNS records, hosting targets, redirects and email records. Changes should be verified carefully to avoid interrupting existing services.</p><a href='/services'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="process"><div class="faq-item-index">061 <span>PROCESS</span></div><details><summary>Can you deploy a website on Vercel?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Static and supported web applications can be deployed on Vercel when build settings, environment variables and project configuration are correct.</p><a href='/services'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="process"><div class="faq-item-index">062 <span>PROCESS</span></div><details><summary>Can you help with GitHub?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>GitHub workflows may include repository organisation, commits, branches, pull requests, deployment connections and troubleshooting build failures.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="process"><div class="faq-item-index">063 <span>PROCESS</span></div><details><summary>What should a project brief include?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Include the problem, target audience, key pages, required features, examples, content availability, budget range, timeline and who will approve the work.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="process"><div class="faq-item-index">064 <span>PROCESS</span></div><details><summary>How are project timelines decided?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Timelines depend on complexity, content readiness, integrations, review cycles and third-party services. A realistic schedule should be agreed after scope is understood.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="process"><div class="faq-item-index">065 <span>PROCESS</span></div><details><summary>Do you offer revisions?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Revision rounds and what counts as a revision should be agreed before work starts so expectations remain clear.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="process"><div class="faq-item-index">066 <span>PROCESS</span></div><details><summary>Can I request changes after launch?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Post-launch changes can be scoped separately. Keep a list of issues, priorities and desired outcomes to make follow-up work efficient.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="process"><div class="faq-item-index">067 <span>PROCESS</span></div><details><summary>Who provides website text and images?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Responsibilities for copy, brand assets, photography and licensing should be agreed at the start. Any supplied assets should be cleared for use.</p><a href='/services'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="process"><div class="faq-item-index">068 <span>PROCESS</span></div><details><summary>Can you use my existing logo?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>An existing logo can usually be incorporated if you have the rights to use it and provide a suitable file format.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="process"><div class="faq-item-index">069 <span>PROCESS</span></div><details><summary>Can you help with branding?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Digital branding may include visual consistency, messaging, typography, colours and profile presentation, based on the existing identity and project goals.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="process"><div class="faq-item-index">070 <span>PROCESS</span></div><details><summary>Can you create social profile links?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>A profile page can link to verified social accounts. Only accounts that belong to the person or brand should be represented as official.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="process"><div class="faq-item-index">071 <span>PROCESS</span></div><details><summary>Where can I find Bakhtawar Khan online?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>You can visit the About.me profile at about.me/muhammadbakhtawar and the Linktree page at linktr.ee/bakhtawark085, alongside the verified profiles listed on this site.</p><a href='/about'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="process"><div class="faq-item-index">072 <span>PROCESS</span></div><details><summary>What is the About.me profile for?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>The About.me page provides another public profile destination for Bakhtawar Khan. Keep its biography and links consistent with the main portfolio.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="process"><div class="faq-item-index">073 <span>PROCESS</span></div><details><summary>What is the Linktree page for?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>The Linktree page can collect selected profile and project links in one place. Check that each destination is current and correctly labelled.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="process"><div class="faq-item-index">074 <span>PROCESS</span></div><details><summary>What is MBK TV?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>MBK TV is one of the digital projects associated with the MBK portfolio. Visit its live site for current features and availability.</p><a href='/about'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="process"><div class="faq-item-index">075 <span>PROCESS</span></div><details><summary>What is MBK Markets?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>MBK Markets is a project exploring a market-data interface. It should not be treated as financial advice or a promise of investment performance.</p><a href='/about'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="process"><div class="faq-item-index">076 <span>PROCESS</span></div><details><summary>What is MBK Downloader?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>MBK Downloader is listed among the portfolio’s web-tool projects. Use services lawfully and respect copyright, platform terms and privacy.</p><a href='/about'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="process"><div class="faq-item-index">077 <span>PROCESS</span></div><details><summary>What is Noor-e-Quran by MBK?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Noor-e-Quran is a faith-related digital project associated with the portfolio. Users should verify religious quotations and references against trusted sources.</p><a href='/about'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="process"><div class="faq-item-index">078 <span>PROCESS</span></div><details><summary>What is Text to Handwriting?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Text to Handwriting is a tool concept that presents typed text in a handwriting-like style. Output quality and available features depend on the current live version.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="process"><div class="faq-item-index">079 <span>PROCESS</span></div><details><summary>Are all projects production-ready?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Not necessarily. Some entries may be experiments or works in progress. Check each project’s live page for its current state and capabilities.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="process"><div class="faq-item-index">080 <span>PROCESS</span></div><details><summary>Can you collaborate with another developer?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Collaboration can be discussed when responsibilities, communication, ownership, review process and deadlines are clear.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="process"><div class="faq-item-index">081 <span>PROCESS</span></div><details><summary>Can you work with international clients?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Remote collaboration may be possible. Time zones, payment arrangements, scope, communication and legal requirements should be discussed before commitment.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="process"><div class="faq-item-index">082 <span>PROCESS</span></div><details><summary>What languages can project content use?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Language requirements should be specified early. Multilingual websites may need translated content, language navigation and appropriate page metadata.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">083 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>Can you make a website bilingual?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>A bilingual website can be planned with translated content, clear language switching and appropriate URL and metadata strategies for each language.</p><a href='/services'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">084 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>How should contact forms handle personal data?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Collect only necessary information, explain how it will be used, protect submissions and provide an appropriate privacy notice.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">085 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>Can you add analytics?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Analytics can be considered when the measurement goals, privacy obligations and consent requirements are understood. Avoid collecting unnecessary personal information.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">086 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>What is a privacy policy?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>A privacy policy explains what personal information is collected, why it is processed, how it is stored or shared and what choices people have.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">087 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>Can you add a cookie banner?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>A consent interface may be needed depending on the technologies used and applicable laws. It should reflect actual tracking behaviour rather than be purely decorative.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">088 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>How should website testimonials be used?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Publish testimonials only with permission and ensure they reflect real feedback. Do not invent reviewers, identities, ratings or customer experiences.</p><a href='/services'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">089 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>Can I leave feedback on a project?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Feedback can be shared through the contact page. Please identify the relevant project and describe what worked well or what should improve.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">090 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>What does human rights mean online?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Digital human rights include privacy, freedom of expression, access to information, non-discrimination and safety, subject to applicable law and the rights of others.</p><a href='/about'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">091 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>How can websites respect human rights?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Use privacy-conscious design, accessible content, clear policies, secure handling of data and respectful moderation. Avoid deceptive patterns and discriminatory treatment.</p><a href='/about'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">092 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>Why is digital privacy important?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Personal information can reveal sensitive details. Collecting less data, limiting access and explaining data use help reduce unnecessary privacy risks.</p><a href='/about'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">093 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>What is responsible AI use?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Responsible AI use involves checking outputs, protecting sensitive data, being transparent about limitations and considering bias, safety and human oversight.</p><a href='/services'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">094 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>How can a website be more inclusive?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Use accessible markup, readable language, keyboard support, sufficient contrast, responsive layouts and respectful content that does not exclude groups of users.</p><a href='/services'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">095 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>How do you handle project confidentiality?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Discuss confidentiality needs before sharing sensitive information. Do not send passwords, private keys, identity documents or confidential customer data through public channels.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">096 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>What happens if a third-party API changes?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>External APIs can change or become unavailable. Robust projects should handle errors, document dependencies and plan for maintenance when necessary.</p><a href='/services'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">097 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>How do you test a website before launch?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Testing can include mobile and desktop layouts, links, forms, keyboard use, accessibility basics, performance, metadata, redirects and key user journeys.</p><a href='/services'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">098 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>What should be checked after a site launches?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Verify the live domain, HTTPS, redirects, page rendering, analytics if used, sitemap, robots rules, forms and Search Console status.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">099 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>Can you guarantee a website will never go down?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>No. Hosting providers, networks, code and third-party services can fail. Monitoring, backups and recovery planning can reduce risk but not eliminate it.</p><a href='/services'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">100 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>How often should website content be updated?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Update content when facts, services, project links or policies change. Accuracy and usefulness matter more than publishing on an arbitrary schedule.</p><a href='/services'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">101 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>How do I report a broken link?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Send the page URL, the broken destination and what you expected to find through the contact page.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">102 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>How can I contact Bakhtawar Khan?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Use the contact page or project enquiry form. Include a short description, relevant links and the best way to respond.</p><a href='/about'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">103 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>What should I include in a first message?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Explain who you are, what you want to achieve, the current situation, important constraints and any deadline. Avoid sending credentials or sensitive personal data.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">104 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>How do I know if a project is a good fit?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>A good fit has a clearly described problem, realistic scope, available inputs, agreed responsibilities and a shared understanding of budget and timing.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">105 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>Do you promise a specific result?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>No result should be promised before requirements and constraints are understood. Search rankings, traffic, conversion rates and third-party uptime are outside any single developer’s full control.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">106 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>How can I keep learning web development?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Build small projects, read official documentation, test your assumptions, review errors and improve one part of a project at a time.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
<article class="faq-item" data-category="projects"><div class="faq-item-index">107 <span>PROJECTS</span></div><details><summary>How can I contribute to an open-source project?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Read the project’s licence and contribution guide, reproduce an issue, make a focused change and explain what you tested.</p><a href='/contact'>Learn more ↗</a></div></details></article>
</div>
<div class="faq-empty" hidden id="faqEmpty"><strong>No matching questions yet.</strong><p>Try another keyword or switch back to all topics.</p><button class="button button-outline" id="faqReset" type="button">Show all questions</button></div>
</section>
